This document is submitted for artifact evaluation for paper #142 at FSE24. Please get in touch with
Yahui Song (yahui_s@nus.edu.sg) for any necessary clarifications. Five checkpoints are highlighted
using **Check Point #n**, claimed from the paper and the appendix.


**1** **STATUS**


We are applying for the Available, Functional, and Reusable badges. Reasons are:

[(1) The Benchmarks](https://zenodo.org/records/10695186) [1] [are available from Zenodo. The Source Code](https://github.com/songyahui/infer_TempFix) [2] of the tool (ProveNFix) is
[available from GitHub. The final version of the Paper](https://www.comp.nus.edu.sg/~yahuis/ProveNFix.pdf) [3] [and the Appendix](https://www.comp.nus.edu.sg/~yahuis/ProveNFix_tr.pdf) [4] are publicly accessible.
(2) The functionality of the artifact can be validated by following the instructions in Sec. 2, which
reproduce the experimental results claimed in the paper (Tables 2-5) and Appendix (C, D, E).
(3) Our artifact is reusable, given the detailed desecration and documentation provided in Sec. 3.

We appreciate your effort in trying out ProveNFix! We would love to hear your feedback!


